      "agreement": "N/A",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Good budget phone with some flaws. Overall this phone is good for the price. It is quite fast, I never notice any lag. Multitasking is instantaneous. The 4gb of internal memory is taken up by a large amount of pre-installed software, mostly google in terms of total megabytes. Rooting allowed me to remove a lot of bloatware with titanium backup, freeing up a lot of space. The screen is very high...",
          "aspect": "camera",
          "sentiment": 0.22179823368787766,
          "stars": 4,
          "month": "2015-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Love it replaced my old Awe phone for this one .... Love it replaced my old Awe phone for this one and it was worth it i love the longer battery life and nice camera",
          "aspect": "camera",
          "sentiment": 0.9981446808669716,
          "stars": 5,
          "month": "2015-04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Good phone but still pocket sized. I've had mine since late October. I use a screen protector (skinomi), and a case with it. I'm coming from a LG Optimus F3, which I rooted. Tried everything under the sun to root it, but at this point, I don't care about that anymore. (Unless someone comes up with an exploit that doesn't cause self destruction... ;) ) Apps in 4.4.2 can use the external SD for...",
          "aspect": "build",
          "sentiment": 0.9928975235670805,
          "stars": 5,
          "month": "2015-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "very impressed. This phone is fantastic for the price (I paid around $50 for it) I like the thin, light design. it is very fast, very easy to use and get started with as it has hands free activation. A little patience and follow the directions-easiest phone to activate ever.. Ive only had it for about a month but I already love love love it.",
          "aspect": "build",
          "sentiment": 0.998409989697393,
          "stars": 5,
          "month": "2015-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "For $40, there's hardly a better phone.. What you think of this phone depends on what you're expecting. I bought it for $40 to replace/upgrade a Samsung Galaxy Reverb. Both phones only have 4 gigs of memory, so that wasn't an upgrade, but the quad-core processor, bigger screen size and Kit Kat all were factors in my decision, along with the price. I love this phone. My Reverb was incredibly slow,...",
          "aspect": "audio",
          "sentiment": 0.587383447214961,
          "stars": 5,
          "month": "2015-02"
        }
      ]
    },
