      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Decent, cheap phone. My first smartphone, I knew this would be cheap and utilitarian going in. I've had this a few months and don't regret the purchase. CONS: A 4GB memory really does limit the app selection; Android 4.4.2 won't let you do much with the SD card storage, so the memory runs out pretty quickly and you have to be very vigilant about moving files and clearing data as you go. Its...",
          "aspect": "audio",
          "sentiment": -0.9872851867694408,
          "stars": 4,
          "month": "2015-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "If you want to cut down on your mobile phone usage, this is the phone for you.. If you want to cut down on your mobile phone usage, this is the phone for you. Set up is simple - but make sure not to slip into accessibility mode or all the buttons become unresponsive. The menu (needed to undo this) is cleverly hidden (hold down the bottom right button for long enough - but you may find this tricky...",
          "aspect": "audio",
          "sentiment": -0.9021614636294544,
          "stars": 1,
          "month": "2015-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Good phone, but limited internal storage. I replaced an HTC One with this phone and I'm so glad I did. I really love this phone and the price was great... I paid $39 but I see the price has gone up now (got mine in March). I would have given it five stars except it has one really irritating flaw... storage space. I don't use many apps and it is constantly telling me I'm about out of space. Using...",
          "aspect": "performance",
          "sentiment": -0.9653867613524199,
          "stars": 4,
          "month": "2015-07"
        },
        {
          "text": "This phone has been a waste of my money. You get what you pay for. I have had the Samsung phones in the past and when I damaged my S3 i bought this as a quick replacement because it was cheap. The camera is not a quality camera at all. The memory seems to always be an issue. I have only downloaded 9 apps and now they don't function correctly. This phone has been a waste of my money.",
          "aspect": "performance",
          "sentiment": -0.9930200978415087,
          "stars": 2,
          "month": "2015-06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mehs. Pro: -Fast -Easy to use, good interfaces and software -Phone hardware is durable (not screen, but I have dropped this thing about 7 times and the hardware itself is still functioning) -Battery lasts the whole day Con: -Not a lot of space for apps and games -Screen is absolute crap, I dropped it on the ground from a height of about 8 inches (it fell down one stair step) and the whole screen...",
          "aspect": "battery",
          "sentiment": -0.11383002996444702,
          "stars": 3,
          "month": "2015-07"
        },
        {
          "text": "I really like this phone. I really like this phone. It's never frozen up on me or anything. The biggest problem I have with it is the internal storage. I take a lot of selfies. So I don't have too much room for other things like app and music and whatnot, even with my sd card. And the battery doesn't last quite as long as I'd like it to. But overall, worth the price. I will be buying another soon...",
          "aspect": "battery",
          "sentiment": -0.9852967946790159,
          "stars": 3,
          "month": "2015-07"
        }
      ]
